<title>USA: U.S. DAP steady on demand, ammonia down slightly.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP steady on demand, ammonia down slightly.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for diammonium phosphate (DAP) and ammonia were steady to slightly lower from Wednesday, cash sources said.</p>
<p>DAP prices were underpinned by export demand from India as well as demand from U.S. farmers, who are just beginning their planting season, dealers said.</p>
<p>			    Dlrs/short ton	 Chg from Wednesday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		175-177	     unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  188-189	     unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		170		   dn 2</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
